If you'd like to do your own research on medical subjects,
then you need "Grateful Med", the access program that allows
you to run searches on literally millions of medical and biology
journal articles. This program (available for both DOS and the MAC)
costs very little (I think about $20) and is extremely powerful.
If you have any interest in medical research (which since you're
reading this newsgroup, you do), you NEED this program.
 
If you or any relative or friend have any medical problems,
this will allow you to get the absolute latest word- including
trials in progress but not yet completed. The average online
search costs me about $5. It searches the MEDLARS databases,
which are the National Library of Medicine databases.
 
I've seen some Life-Extension companies offer to run a MEDLARS
search for $50 for one topic. For that money, you could buy the
program and conduct 10 or 20 searches. Incidentally, when you
duy the program, you get a few hours of free on-line search time.
 
What this program will do is get you the citation, and abstract
if available. To get full text of articles you're interested in,
there's a feature called "lonesome doc", which allows you while
still on-line, to order copies of articles from a nearby medical
library that you've set up an account with.
 
HIGHLY RECCOMMENDED.
 
You can get information on how to order "Grateful Med" from:
1-800-638-8480
email to: gmhelp@gmedserv.nlm.nih.gov



